WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:06.900
This is Allen Company training on how you'll be

00:06.900 --> 00:09.588
warned of a fire underground, and what to do when

00:09.588 --> 00:12.888
you are. In an underground mine, smoke and carbon

00:12.888 --> 00:15.838
monoxide travel with the air. People far from a

00:15.838 --> 00:18.888
fire can be in danger before they see or smell

00:18.888 --> 00:21.775
any smoke. That's why every underground mine has

00:21.775 --> 00:24.825
a fire alarm system that can promptly warn everyone

00:24.825 --> 00:25.800
underground.

00:26.916 --> 00:29.954
If anyone works beyond where the system can reach,

00:29.954 --> 00:32.254
the mine has to have another way to warn them.

00:32.254 --> 00:34.354
Know which method covers your work area.

00:37.678 --> 00:40.578
Many underground mines use stench gas as the fire

00:40.578 --> 00:43.078
warning. A strong-smelling chemical,

00:43.078 --> 00:46.428
usually ethyl mercaptan, smells like rotten eggs

00:46.428 --> 00:49.628
or cabbage. At every Allen underground mine,

00:49.628 --> 00:52.628
it's released into the intake fan, and the ventilation

00:52.628 --> 00:55.053
carries it to every working place.

00:56.176 --> 00:59.101
If you smell stench gas, it means evacuate.

00:59.101 --> 01:01.663
Don't wait to see if it's real. Stop work,

01:01.663 --> 01:04.276
shut down your equipment in a safe position,

01:04.276 --> 01:06.476
make sure your self-rescuer is with you,

01:06.476 --> 01:08.713
and head out by your assigned escape route.

01:08.713 --> 01:11.813
If you smell smoke or feel heat in your self-rescuer,

01:11.813 --> 01:12.739
put it on.

01:13.858 --> 01:16.533
At our mines, the stench is backed up by radio

01:16.533 --> 01:19.620
calls and strobe lights. Your supervisor will show

01:19.620 --> 01:21.008
you where the strobes are.

01:24.332 --> 01:26.882
Every underground mine has at least two separate

01:26.882 --> 01:30.007
escapeways to the surface, and a written escape

01:30.007 --> 01:33.219
and evacuation plan that's posted. Learn your primary

01:33.219 --> 01:35.394
and secondary routes from where you work,

01:35.394 --> 01:36.595
and how they're marked.

01:37.718 --> 01:39.905
When you reach the surface, go to the gathering

01:39.905 --> 01:42.493
point and check out on the tag board so everyone

01:42.493 --> 01:45.568
is accounted for. Never go back in for anyone;

01:45.568 --> 01:47.656
tell the person in charge who's missing.

01:48.776 --> 01:52.113
Evacuation drills are held at least every six months,

01:52.113 --> 01:54.613
on each shift, and they include setting off the

01:54.613 --> 01:58.126
fire alarm. Treat every drill like the real thing.

02:01.458 --> 02:04.108
On the surface, the fire warning at every Allen

02:04.108 --> 02:07.158
site is a radio call. Learn the gathering point

02:07.158 --> 02:10.008
at your site; at most Allen quarries it's the tag

02:10.008 --> 02:10.695
board.

02:11.820 --> 02:15.032
Recap: smoke and CO travel with the air.

02:15.032 --> 02:18.357
Stench gas means get out, now. Shut down safely,

02:18.357 --> 02:21.820
keep your W65 with you, use your escapeway,

02:21.820 --> 02:23.458
and check out at the surface.

02:24.582 --> 02:27.744
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

02:27.744 --> 02:29.245
override this video.
